   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2016, CDC and Standard Chartered signed a risk participation agreement to support new working capital lending of up to $30 million to businesses in Sierra Leone. This followed a 2015 risk participation agreement where both organisations had agreed to provide working capital lending of up to $50 million ($25 million each) to the country&#xED;s businesses to support the country&#xED;s recovery from the Ebola crisis.</narrative>
   </description>
